This page shows the client portal from the client's side. The presenter signs in as Rachel Lau Pei Qi, the finance contact of Marigold Lane Kitchen Pte. Ltd., and the tenant admin of the firm reads her sign-in code.

The firm has already opened the portal for Marigold Lane Kitchen on the company's **Client Portal** tab in CRM, turned on the modules and invited Rachel. Rachel is a **Company admin** of the company in the portal.

## Sign in as Rachel

Rachel has no password. She signs in with a code sent by email, and in the demo environment that email goes to the firm's **Demo inbox**. Only the tenant admin can open the demo inbox, so use two browser windows: one signed in as the firm's admin, and a private window for the portal.

{% steps %}
1. In the private window, open `https://demo.operoncore.app/portal/login`.
2. Select **Email me a sign-in code**, type `<prefix>.client@demo.operoncore.app` and select **Send code**.
3. In the other window, sign in as `<prefix>.admin@demo.operoncore.app`. Select the avatar at the bottom of the side bar, then **Demo inbox**, and open the newest email to Rachel's address. Select **Refresh** if it is not listed yet.
4. Back in the portal, type the code in **6-digit code** and select **Continue**. The code works for 10 minutes and can be used once.
{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-sign-in-code" caption="Portal sign-in with an emailed code." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Difference from the live service" %}
On the live service the code goes to the client's own mailbox. In the demo environment no email leaves Operon; the code is only in the demo inbox.
{% /aside %}

If a person has access to more than one company, the portal first asks them to choose one under **Companies**. They can switch at any time with **Switch** at the top of the side bar.

## Find your way around

Every page has the same frame:

- **Side bar.** At the top, the company that is open and **Switch**. Below it, **Home**, **To-do** and **Messages**, then the company's modules under **Company**: **Invoices**, **Accounting & Tax**, **Secretarial**, **E-sign** and **Documents**. A module appears only if the firm turned it on. At the bottom, **Serviced by** names the firm.
- **Top bar.** **Search** looks through invoices, cases, documents and the other modules (type at least 2 characters). The bell opens **Notifications**. The avatar opens **My account** and **Sign out**.
- **Status colours.** The same colours are used on every page: orange **Needs you**, red **Failed** or **Overdue**, blue for something that is with the firm, and green **Completed**, **Delivered** or **Signed**.

## Home

After sign-in the portal opens **Home**: a greeting, the company and today's date in Singapore time, and four tiles: **Waiting on you**, **To sign**, **Questions from your accountant** and **Unread messages**. Select a tile to filter the board below it.

Below the tiles are the key figures that the firm keeps for the company, such as **Owed to you**, **GST payable** and **Books closed to**, and the deadlines under **Coming up**.

The **Waiting on you** board lists everything Rachel has to do, with **Item**, **Module**, **Status** and **Due**. Each row has one action: **Answer**, **Sign**, **Fix** or **Open**. **Done recently** lists what was finished in the last days. **Recent activity** on the right shows what happened in the company's portal, such as a new message, a shared file or a delivered invoice.

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-home" caption="The portal home page of Marigold Lane Kitchen." /%}

## To-do

Open **To-do**. It holds the same items as **Waiting on you**, grouped by module. **Overdue** and **This week** count what is late and what is due soon. Use **This company** and **All companies** to choose whether the list shows only Marigold Lane Kitchen or every company Rachel can open.

## E-sign

Open **E-sign**. Three tiles count **Waiting for your signature**, **Waiting for others** and **Completed**, and the documents are grouped below them. This page lists documents for every company Rachel can open, so each row names its company.

Under **Waiting for your signature** is the engagement letter for bookkeeping, GST and payroll for the financial year ending 31 December 2027, sent by Daniel Ong. Select **Sign** to sign it online. After signing, it moves to **Completed**, and **Download** gives the signed copy.

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-esign-waiting" caption="The engagement letter waiting for Rachel's signature." /%}

## Documents

Open **Documents**. The path at the top starts at **Home**. Under **Folders** is **Shared with Marigold Lane**, which the accountant shared with the client. It holds the FY2025 financial statements and the GST F5 acknowledgement for July to September 2026. Open the folder and select a file to open or download it.

Select **Upload** to send a file to the firm. What Rachel uploads is kept in **Your uploads**. **Search file names** finds a file in any folder.

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-documents-folder" caption="The folder the firm shared with the client." /%}

## Accounting & Tax

Open **Accounting & Tax**. **Owed to you** at the top shows what the company's customers still owe it, from the invoices the firm has recorded. The filters **Needs you**, **With** Larkspur Corporate Services and **Completed** narrow the list of cases. Each case shows its **Period**, what is **Waiting on you** and its **Status**.

Select **Open** on the bookkeeping case. The case page shows how many questions are done, and the questions from the accountant. Two are **To answer**:

- the October and November bank statements for the Corallis Bank account ending 7726;
- this quarter's supplier invoices so far.

Type a reply in **Your answer**, attach a file with **Attach** if needed, and select **Send**. The question becomes **Answered**. An answer cannot be changed after it is sent; Rachel can add something in **Messages**. On the firm's side, the reply appears in the company's bookkeeping case.

On the right, **Handled by** names the accountant, with a **Message** button. Under **Anything else for this period?**, **Choose files** sends more documents for the books.

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-accounting-questions" caption="Questions from the firm, waiting for an answer." /%}

## Messages

Open **Messages**. The conversation with the firm already has three messages between Daniel Ong and Rachel about the GST return and the engagement letter. Type in the message box, attach a file with **Attach** if needed, and select **Send**. On the firm's side, the message appears on the company's **Messages** tab in CRM.

On the right, **Your team at** Larkspur Corporate Services lists the people at the firm who look after the company, and **People at your company** lists everyone at Marigold Lane Kitchen who can read the conversation.

## Secretarial: the checklist

Open **Secretarial**. The checklist for the new director of Marigold Lane Kitchen is listed with the status **Needs you**. Select **Open**. Each item shows **Done** or **To fill**, and the bar at the top counts how many are done. Two answers are already filled in: the date the appointment takes effect, and that no director is stepping down. Fill in the rest live:

{% steps %}
1. Under **New director**, select **Add a person**. Type **Full name (as in the passport or NRIC)** `Clement Yeo Shao Wen`, **Email** `clement.yeo@marigoldlane.example` and **Mobile** `+65 5201 3368`. With **Add a file**, upload first `02-checklist/Clement Yeo NRIC front (specimen).pdf` and then `02-checklist/Clement Yeo NRIC back (specimen).pdf` from the [demo files](/en/demo/overview/#demo-files), unchanged.
2. Optional: under the board approval item, attach `02-checklist/Marigold Lane board resolution - new director (specimen).pdf` with **Add a file**.
3. Select **Send to Larkspur Corporate Services** at the top, then **Submit** in **Submit these answers?**.
{% /steps %}

The checklist shows **Sent to us**, and Rachel cannot change the answers unless the firm sends an item back. A file that Rachel uploads to the checklist can be opened only by her; other people at her company see who uploaded it. The firm's side of this checklist is on [Secretarial: the client checklist](/en/demo/client-checklist/).

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-checklist-open" caption="The new-director checklist, with two answers already given." /%}

## Invoices: InvoiceNow

The firm registered Marigold Lane Kitchen and Tidewater Studio for InvoiceNow, so the two companies can send InvoiceNow invoices to each other. Open **Invoices**. The strip at the top counts **Draft**, **Sending**, **Not delivered**, **Delivered this month** and **Received this month**. The tabs are **All**, **Draft**, **Sent**, **Not delivered**, **Credit notes** and **Received**. The **Delivery** column shows where each sent document is.

**Received.** Two documents from Tidewater Studio:

| Document | What it is |
|---|---|
| Invoice TWS-2026-045 | Menu redesign, food photography and two sets of printed table cards, with 9% GST, Net 30. |
| Credit note TWS-CN-2026-003 | One set of table cards credited back, because the print run was cancelled. |

Open a document to see **Received document**, and select **Download original** for the original file.

{% aside type="note" title="Received documents arrive within 15 minutes" %}
The two received documents are sent when the account is opened or reset, and they appear in **Received** within about 15 minutes. Right after a reset the tab can still be empty.
{% /aside %}

**Send the draft live.** Under **Draft** is an invoice from Marigold Lane Kitchen to Tidewater Studio for catering the studio's open house (60 guests and service staff, Net 14, buyer reference TWS-PO-2611).

{% steps %}
1. Open the draft. Check the buyer, the details, the lines, the totals and the preview.
2. Select **Send**, then **Send** in **Send this document?**.
3. Open **Sent**. The **Delivery** column shows **On its way**, and after about a minute a tick with the delivery time.
{% /steps %}

The invoice is delivered to Tidewater Studio over the mock Access Point. If a document cannot be delivered, its row is marked **Failed** with a short reason, and **Copy to a new draft** starts a corrected copy. A sent document cannot be changed.

**New** starts an invoice or a credit note. **Invoice settings** › **Design** shows Marigold Lane Kitchen's own invoice design: its colour and its Corallis Bank payment details.

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-invoicenow-received" caption="The Received tab, with an invoice and a credit note from Tidewater Studio." /%}

{% screenshot id="demo/portal-invoicenow-delivered" caption="The draft sent live, delivered." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Difference from the live service" %}
In the demo environment InvoiceNow uses a mock Access Point. Registration is approved at once, and a sent document is delivered about ten seconds after it is sent. Nothing reaches the Peppol network.
{% /aside %}

## My account

Select the avatar at the top right, then **My account**:

- **Language**: **English** or **中文**. This changes the portal for Rachel on every device. It does not depend on the browser's language.
- **Password**: Rachel signs in with an emailed code. **Set a password** lets her sign in with a password as well; Operon emails a link to set it.
- **Authenticator app**: adds a second step at sign-in.
- **Sign out everywhere**: signs Rachel out on every device, including this one.

The email address she signs in with is managed by the firm and cannot be changed here.
